Time Complexity
O(N*M), where N is the number of rows and M is the number of columns. The algorithm iterates through every cell in the grid once during the nested initialization loops and visits each land cell exactly once during the DFS traversal. Inserting a shape into the set takes O(K*log(S)), where K is the number of cells in the island and S is the number of distinct islands.
Space Complexity
O(N*M). This includes the O(N*M) space for the 'vis' matrix, the O(N*M) space for the recursion stack in the worst-case scenario (a grid fully filled with 1s), and the O(N*M) space used to store the distinct island shapes in the 'st' set.

